{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1092"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge technology/computing","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/technology__computing.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",230],["-","2006."],["+","2006"],["=",1],["+","by Dorsey himself – the first tweet, the name that stuck for every publicly readable short message on the service. "],["=",42],["-","SMS,"],["+","SMS"],["=",1],["+","(in November 2017 it was doubled to 280 characters), "],["=",351],["+"," Its origin story also ended up in court: the Harvard twins Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss, who had asked Zuckerberg in 2003 to program their own campus network, later called ConnectU, sued him in 2004 for allegedly stealing their idea. In 2008 they settled with Mark Zuckerberg's company for a package worth about 65 million dollars, a dispute later retold in the film „The Social Network“."],["=",454]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",212],["-","verschickt."],["+","von"],["=",1],["+","Dorsey selbst verschickt – der erste Tweet, wie seither jede öffentlich lesbare Kurznachricht des Dienstes heißt. "],["=",38],["-","SMS,"],["+","SMS"],["=",1],["+","(im November 2017 wurde sie auf 280 Zeichen verdoppelt), "],["=",345],["+"," Seine Gründungsgeschichte landete auch vor Gericht: Die Harvard-Zwillinge Cameron und Tyler Winklevoss, die Zuckerberg 2003 gebeten hatten, ihr eigenes Campus-Netzwerk zu programmieren, das spätere ConnectU, verklagten ihn 2004, weil er ihre Idee gestohlen haben soll. 2008 einigten sie sich mit dem Unternehmen von Mark Zuckerberg auf ein Paket im Wert von rund 65 Millionen Dollar – ein Streit, den später der Film „The Social Network“ nacherzählte."],["=",436]]}]},
